its about the git basic essensials ;

there are three levels to push a file in a repository;

they are,
    *git init --- initialize
    *git add --- add a file to the folder
    *git commit -m ""  --- save the file stanby in the local repo
    *git push --- push the file to the remote repo
    *git pull --- pull the file from the repo
    *git clone <https://repo> --- clone the remote repo to the folder
    *git log --- used to see the changes 
    *git status --- used to see which file is tracked and are not ,modified etc..
    *git remote set-url <URL> --- to change the repo
    *git remote -v --- to see which repo are we in.
    *git branch --- to see which branch are we in (main,master)
    *git --oneline --- used to see the log in one line
    *restore --- Restore working tree files
    *revert --- Revert some existing commits 
with this basics we can create a repo and maintain version controll



